[[:db/retract 17592186184778 :question/answer-fields 17592186183277] {:db/id 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f6dcfad9-4fa8-567a-ab9a-f61e9f6b1a76" "question-0f199eb7-3af6-57bb-a681-cef6be591a7a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f6dcfad9-4fa8-567a-ab9a-f61e9f6b1a76" :question/id #uuid "f6dcfad9-4fa8-567a-ab9a-f61e9f6b1a76" :question/math-academy-id "q-39856" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$  \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{16}\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d5f218f-38ba-531a-af9e-df5b58a66d01"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d5f218f-38ba-531a-af9e-df5b58a66d01" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5f218f-38ba-531a-af9e-df5b58a66d01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5170028a-ab43-580a-a8b5-29da72f1fcd9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c4a4aea-dd6d-5e0a-99e0-02a535cf0fc4" "answer-f37da0e2-81e8-576a-aa5e-b3594802c8da" "answer-5170028a-ab43-580a-a8b5-29da72f1fcd9" "answer-2fef03fc-79ed-52dc-bd31-1e9cf734dd91" "answer-c52aa776-edc2-57f3-a183-a9201feae1aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c4a4aea-dd6d-5e0a-99e0-02a535cf0fc4" :answer/id #uuid "7c4a4aea-dd6d-5e0a-99e0-02a535cf0fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f37da0e2-81e8-576a-aa5e-b3594802c8da" :answer/id #uuid "f37da0e2-81e8-576a-aa5e-b3594802c8da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5170028a-ab43-580a-a8b5-29da72f1fcd9" :answer/id #uuid "5170028a-ab43-580a-a8b5-29da72f1fcd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fef03fc-79ed-52dc-bd31-1e9cf734dd91" :answer/id #uuid "2fef03fc-79ed-52dc-bd31-1e9cf734dd91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c52aa776-edc2-57f3-a183-a9201feae1aa" :answer/id #uuid "c52aa776-edc2-57f3-a183-a9201feae1aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-15ea3713-dc0a-53ca-b70c-c22a6b79a105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184778 :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-9{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4bd4b417-69d9-54a6-aef3-a9bc3d8656f8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4bd4b417-69d9-54a6-aef3-a9bc3d8656f8" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bd4b417-69d9-54a6-aef3-a9bc3d8656f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8b4af8f4-7d15-5294-891c-2810e7b0aee5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09f25da8-1536-541d-983b-95cee16bd959" "answer-4e40efb6-25f0-52a4-b9bd-0bfe176c7b25" "answer-be33eccb-cb9a-5eb3-8bb8-2724f8b921de" "answer-8b4af8f4-7d15-5294-891c-2810e7b0aee5" "answer-a6a69985-146d-572c-8484-4f24cfb9840f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09f25da8-1536-541d-983b-95cee16bd959" :answer/id #uuid "09f25da8-1536-541d-983b-95cee16bd959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e40efb6-25f0-52a4-b9bd-0bfe176c7b25" :answer/id #uuid "4e40efb6-25f0-52a4-b9bd-0bfe176c7b25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be33eccb-cb9a-5eb3-8bb8-2724f8b921de" :answer/id #uuid "be33eccb-cb9a-5eb3-8bb8-2724f8b921de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b4af8f4-7d15-5294-891c-2810e7b0aee5" :answer/id #uuid "8b4af8f4-7d15-5294-891c-2810e7b0aee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6a69985-146d-572c-8484-4f24cfb9840f" :answer/id #uuid "a6a69985-146d-572c-8484-4f24cfb9840f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15ea3713-dc0a-53ca-b70c-c22a6b79a105" :question/id #uuid "15ea3713-dc0a-53ca-b70c-c22a6b79a105" :question/math-academy-id "q-86853" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9de09353-fb9c-544f-8c67-c4ef2c4abd36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9de09353-fb9c-544f-8c67-c4ef2c4abd36" :answer-field/id #uuid "9de09353-fb9c-544f-8c67-c4ef2c4abd36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-453ed560-2a6a-584b-b775-2ac6a73e45b3" "answer-75d24566-becf-5714-8a17-ca7340070ab8" "answer-b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" "answer-a4e29b1a-ee23-527d-a4ce-26194d144439" "answer-4e677ef6-4718-55df-b04f-5323f885a475"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-453ed560-2a6a-584b-b775-2ac6a73e45b3" :answer/id #uuid "453ed560-2a6a-584b-b775-2ac6a73e45b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75d24566-becf-5714-8a17-ca7340070ab8" :answer/id #uuid "75d24566-becf-5714-8a17-ca7340070ab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" :answer/id #uuid "b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4e29b1a-ee23-527d-a4ce-26194d144439" :answer/id #uuid "a4e29b1a-ee23-527d-a4ce-26194d144439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e677ef6-4718-55df-b04f-5323f885a475" :answer/id #uuid "4e677ef6-4718-55df-b04f-5323f885a475" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d93f91c3-07ee-5843-9236-38543eb4a92a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d93f91c3-07ee-5843-9236-38543eb4a92a" :question/id #uuid "d93f91c3-07ee-5843-9236-38543eb4a92a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139474" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(6-0)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b507b6b-07ae-51ff-8ef0-2463cc379cda"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b507b6b-07ae-51ff-8ef0-2463cc379cda" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b507b6b-07ae-51ff-8ef0-2463cc379cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b038fe34-a16a-5a55-bf98-fc3b8439343d" "answer-29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" "answer-d9c0d55a-c5e9-50c2-8df7-9355a909c1d6" "answer-f15ad28f-93e2-5d8b-b5d3-7600366bd867" "answer-66516586-cecd-5e63-b1f0-d497a546cd06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b038fe34-a16a-5a55-bf98-fc3b8439343d" :answer/id #uuid "b038fe34-a16a-5a55-bf98-fc3b8439343d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" :answer/id #uuid "29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9c0d55a-c5e9-50c2-8df7-9355a909c1d6" :answer/id #uuid "d9c0d55a-c5e9-50c2-8df7-9355a909c1d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f15ad28f-93e2-5d8b-b5d3-7600366bd867" :answer/id #uuid "f15ad28f-93e2-5d8b-b5d3-7600366bd867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66516586-cecd-5e63-b1f0-d497a546cd06" :answer/id #uuid "66516586-cecd-5e63-b1f0-d497a546cd06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f199eb7-3af6-57bb-a681-cef6be591a7a" :question/id #uuid "0f199eb7-3af6-57bb-a681-cef6be591a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139476" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 18\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a54a21cb-93a2-537e-bb2f-71cc7631af9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a54a21cb-93a2-537e-bb2f-71cc7631af9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a54a21cb-93a2-537e-bb2f-71cc7631af9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-10c81834-42ef-5852-b301-a6d3cbb3c8fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd6421c2-2bc0-520a-be99-675b8f795b1c" "answer-9f06a3b6-8e48-5d5d-b47c-2bf33ee89c30" "answer-970d7f5e-257f-5c6c-a87e-441a641de9a7" "answer-10c81834-42ef-5852-b301-a6d3cbb3c8fb" "answer-fb4520b1-1d35-57bb-b9ad-3e48af9ee8cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd6421c2-2bc0-520a-be99-675b8f795b1c" :answer/id #uuid "fd6421c2-2bc0-520a-be99-675b8f795b1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f06a3b6-8e48-5d5d-b47c-2bf33ee89c30" :answer/id #uuid "9f06a3b6-8e48-5d5d-b47c-2bf33ee89c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-970d7f5e-257f-5c6c-a87e-441a641de9a7" :answer/id #uuid "970d7f5e-257f-5c6c-a87e-441a641de9a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10c81834-42ef-5852-b301-a6d3cbb3c8fb" :answer/id #uuid "10c81834-42ef-5852-b301-a6d3cbb3c8fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb4520b1-1d35-57bb-b9ad-3e48af9ee8cf" :answer/id #uuid "fb4520b1-1d35-57bb-b9ad-3e48af9ee8cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c9eb477d-ec3c-5256-a223-de788147d2e5" :activity/id #uui